# 必考词 Unit02
# 领域: 考研
# 学科: 英语词汇
# 来源: 2023红宝书考研英语词汇-必考词
# 描述: 必考词Unit02核心高频词汇

{{announce}}{/əˈnaʊns/}{{v. 宣布；通知}}{{The company announced a new product launch at the conference.}}

{{annual}}{/ˈænjuəl/}{{adj. 每年的；n. 年刊}}{{The company holds an annual meeting every December.}}

{{anonymous}}{/əˈnɒnɪməs/}{{adj. 匿名的}}{{The donation was made by an anonymous benefactor.}}

{{anticipate}}{/ænˈtɪsɪpeɪt/}{{v. 预期；期望}}{{We anticipate a significant increase in demand.}}

{{apparent}}{/əˈpærənt/}{{adj. 明显的；表面上的}}{{It was apparent that the experiment had failed.}}

{{appeal}}{/əˈpiːl/}{{v./n. 呼吁；上诉；吸引}}{{The idea of working abroad appeals to many young people.}}

{{appliance}}{/əˈplaɪəns/}{{n. 器具；家用电器}}{{The kitchen is equipped with modern appliances.}}

{{applicable}}{/əˈplɪkəbl/}{{adj. 适用的；可应用的}}{{This rule is applicable to all employees.}}

{{applicant}}{/ˈæplɪkənt/}{{n. 申请人}}{{Over 200 applicants applied for the position.}}

{{appoint}}{/əˈpɔɪnt/}{{v. 任命；约定}}{{He was appointed as the new director of the department.}}

{{appreciate}}{/əˈpriːʃieɪt/}{{v. 欣赏；感激；理解}}{{I really appreciate your help during this difficult time.}}

{{approach}}{/əˈprəʊtʃ/}}{v. 接近；n. 方法}}{{We need to adopt a new approach to solve this problem.}}

{{appropriate}}{/əˈprəʊpriət/}{{adj. 适当的；合适的}}{{Please wear appropriate clothing for the formal event.}}

{{approve}}{/əˈpruːv/}{{v. 批准；赞成}}{{The committee approved the proposal unanimously.}}

{{arise}}{/əˈraɪz/}{{v. 出现；产生}}{{Problems may arise during the implementation of the plan.}}

{{arouse}}{/əˈraʊz/}{{v. 唤起；引起}}{{The speech aroused great enthusiasm among the audience.}}

{{artificial}}{/ˌɑːrtɪˈfɪʃl/}{{adj. 人工的；人造的}}{{Artificial intelligence is transforming many industries.}}

{{aspect}}{/ˈæspekt/}{{n. 方面；角度}}{{We need to consider every aspect of the problem.}}

{{assault}}{/əˈsɔːlt/}{{n./v. 攻击；袭击}}{{The soldiers launched an assault on the enemy position.}}

{{assemble}}{/əˈsembl/}{{v. 集合；组装}}{{The workers assembled the parts in the factory.}}

{{assert}}{/əˈsɜːrt/}{{v. 断言；主张}}{{He asserted his innocence throughout the trial.}}

{{assess}}{/əˈses/}{{v. 评估；评定}}{{The teacher assessed the students' performance through exams.}}

{{asset}}{/ˈæset/}{{n. 资产；有用的东西}}{{Good communication skills are a valuable asset in business.}}

{{assign}}{/əˈsaɪn/}{{v. 分配；指派}}{{The manager assigned the task to the most experienced team member.}}

{{assist}}{/əˈsɪst/}{{v. 帮助；协助}}{{The nurse assisted the doctor during the operation.}}

{{associate}}{/əˈsəʊʃieɪt/}{{v. 联系；n. 合伙人}}{{People often associate the color red with passion.}}

{{assume}}{/əˈsjuːm/}{{v. 假设；承担}}{{We cannot assume that the results will be the same next time.}}

{{assure}}{/əˈʃʊər/}{{v. 保证；使确信}}{{I assure you that the product is of high quality.}}

{{atmosphere}}{/ˈætməsfɪər/}{{n. 大气；气氛}}{{The restaurant has a warm and friendly atmosphere.}}

{{attach}}{/əˈtætʃ/}{{v. 附上；依恋}}{{Please attach your resume to the email.}}

{{attain}}{/əˈteɪn/}{{v. 达到；获得}}{{She attained the highest score in the exam.}}

{{attempt}}{/əˈtempt/}}{v./n. 尝试；企图}}{{He attempted to climb the mountain but failed.}}

{{attend}}{/əˈtend/}{{v. 出席；照料}}{{All members are expected to attend the meeting.}}

{{attitude}}{/ˈætɪtjuːd/}{{n. 态度；看法}}{{A positive attitude is important for success.}}

{{attract}}{/əˈtrækt/}{{v. 吸引；引起}}{{The beautiful scenery attracts millions of tourists every year.}}

{{attribute}}{/əˈtrɪbjuːt/}{{v. 归因于；n. 属性}}{{She attributed her success to hard work and determination.}}

{{authority}}{/ɔːˈθɒrəti/}{{n. 权威；当局}}{{The local authority decided to build a new hospital.}}

{{automatic}}{/ˌɔːtəˈmætɪk/}{{adj. 自动的；无意识的}}{{The door has an automatic locking system.}}

{{available}}{/əˈveɪləbl/}{{adj. 可用的；有空的}}{{The report is available on the company website.}}

{{aware}}{/əˈweər/}{{adj. 意识到的；知道的}}{{Many people are not aware of the risks of climate change.}}
